    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\nThe change followed the codebase's existing pattern for derived owner fields (like `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `identityKey`), which are defined in the OpenAPI schema and computed via MapStruct mapping expressions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and it's serialized in the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` and a `checkDigit(Owner)` method that runs the standard Luhn algorithm over the digits of `customerCode` (rightmost digit doubled first, non-digits skipped), matching the reference `luhn(...)` the test uses to compute its expectation.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact `checkDigit` \u2014 passes, and the full suite is green.",
